WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.457
This glossary gives you a compact review.

00:00:02.457 --> 00:00:05.067
Do not memorize every sentence exactly.

00:00:05.067 --> 00:00:09.932
The important skill is being able to distinguish the terms when you encounter a new dataset.

00:00:09.932 --> 00:00:16.707
If you can explain structured versus semi-structured, nominal versus ordinal, interval versus ratio,

00:00:16.707 --> 00:00:21.897
and discrete versus continuous, you have the conceptual foundation for the next module.

00:00:21.897 --> 00:00:24.432
Do not treat this as a list to memorize.

00:00:24.432 --> 00:00:29.077
Try to explain each idea using one example from a project you understand.

00:00:29.077 --> 00:00:31.772
If you can describe when you would use the concept, what assumption it makes,

00:00:31.772 --> 00:00:37.016
and how you would validate the result, you are ready to apply it independently.
